<title>UK: BP in Philippines solar package pact.</title>
<headline>BP in Philippines solar package pact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc said on Monday it had signed a three-year contract with the Philippines government to install solar systems in remote villages of the country.</p>
<p>The project, worth nearly $30 million, will be funded by way of a concessional loan provided by the Australian Export Finance and Insurance Corp.</p>
<p>Under the deal, BP Solar will install more than 1,000 packaged solar systems in over 400 villages in the Visayas and Mindanao regions of the country.</p>
<p>The packages will be made at BP Solar's factory in Sydney, providing more than 40 new jobs in Australia, BP said in a statement. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
